  "macroOverview": "PCE April printed 3.80% annual change (up from 3.50% in March), the hottest reading of 2026, cementing the higher-for-longer Fed narrative. FOMC minutes released Wed 27 May confirmed a fractured committee: Hammack, Kashkari, and Logan form an explicit hawkish bloc rejecting near-term cuts and flagging oil-driven inflation. GDP Q1 second estimate revised to 2.0% annualized (BEA). NAS100 reached a new ATH of 30,470 Friday -- first-ever sustained close above 30,000 on AI capex momentum. US30 broke to new year high 51,094. Gold crashed to 4,363 on FOMC hawkish reaction then recovered to 4,593 on Iran ceasefire extension reports. The broken support zone 4,635-4,650 held as firm resistance for the third time. RBA Wed Jun 3 (4th +25bp consensus), BoC Thu Jun 4 (40% cut probability), and NFP Fri Jun 5 dominate the week ahead.",
